## b. How to Set Up the Backend and Frontend

Environment assumptions:
- Backend exposed on http://localhost:3000
- Frontend served on http://localhost:5173 (Vite dev) or via static hosting (production)

Directory layout:
- Root: course-project/
  - backend/
  - frontend/

### 1) Backend Setup

1. Configure environment variables in [backend/.env](backend/.env):
   - JWT_SECRET=your_secret_here
   - EMAIL_USER=your_gmail_username
   - EMAIL_PASSWORD=your_app_password
   - FRONTEND_URL=http://localhost:5173

2. Install dependencies:
   - From [backend](backend) folder:
     ```sh
     npm install
     ```

3. Initialize Prisma and database:
   - Ensure SQLite is available (default). If using another DB, update [backend/prisma/schema.prisma](backend/prisma/schema.prisma) accordingly.
   - Run migrations:
     ```sh
     npx prisma migrate deploy
     ```
   - Seed data:
     ```sh
     npm run seed
     ```

4. Start backend:
   - Development (auto-restart):
     ```sh
     npx nodemon index.js 3000
     ```
   - Production:
     ```sh
     node index.js 3000
     ```

The server will be available at http://localhost:3000. Ensure CORS matches FRONTEND_URL.

### 2) Frontend Setup

1. Configure environment variables in [frontend/.env](frontend/.env):
   - VITE_BACKEND_URL=http://localhost:3000

2. Install dependencies:
   - From [frontend](frontend) folder:
     ```sh
     npm install
     ```

3. Run development server:
   ```sh
   npm run dev
   ```
   - Default URL: http://localhost:5173

4. Build for production:
   ```sh
   npm run build
   ```
   - Output in [frontend/dist](frontend/dist)

## c. Deployment Information

i. Recommended: Run backend and frontend on the same VM for simplicity.

Example environment:
- OS: Ubuntu 20.04 LTS
- CPU: 2 vCPU
- RAM: 4 GB
- Disk: 20 GB
- Node.js: 18+
- Reverse proxy: Nginx

### Production Deployment (Single VM)

1. Backend (Express + Prisma):
   - Create a systemd service (optional) to manage the backend:
     ```ini
     [Unit]
     Description=UTORAwards Backend
     After=network.target

     [Service]
     Type=simple
     WorkingDirectory=/var/www/course-project/backend
     ExecStart=/usr/bin/node index.js 3001
     Restart=always
     Environment=NODE_ENV=production
     Environment=JWT_SECRET=your_secret_here
     Environment=EMAIL_USER=your_gmail_username
     Environment=EMAIL_PASSWORD=your_app_password
     Environment=FRONTEND_URL=https://your-frontend-domain

     [Install]
     WantedBy=multi-user.target
     ```

   - Enable and start:
     ```sh
     sudo systemctl enable utorawards-backend
     sudo systemctl start utorawards-backend
     ```

2. Frontend (Vite build + Nginx static hosting):
   - Build assets:
     ```sh
     cd frontend
     npm run build
     ```
   - Copy [frontend/dist](frontend/dist) to Nginx web root (e.g., /var/www/utorawards/dist).
   - Nginx config (example):
     ```nginx
     server {
       listen 80;
       server_name your-frontend-domain;

       root /var/www/utorawards/dist;
       index index.html;

       location / {
         try_files $uri /index.html;
       }

       # Proxy API to backend
       location /uploads/ {
         proxy_pass http://127.0.0.1:3001/uploads/;
         proxy_set_header Host $host;
       }

       location /auth/ {
         proxy_pass http://127.0.0.1:3001/auth/;
       }
       location /users/ {
         proxy_pass http://127.0.0.1:3001/users/;
       }
       location /events/ {
         proxy_pass http://127.0.0.1:3001/events/;
       }
       location /transactions/ {
         proxy_pass http://127.0.0.1:3001/transactions/;
       }
       location /promotions/ {
         proxy_pass http://127.0.0.1:3001/promotions/;
       }
     }
     ```

3. Environment variables:
   - Backend [backend/.env](backend/.env) must set FRONTEND_URL to your public frontend URL.
   - Frontend [frontend/.env](frontend/.env) must set VITE_BACKEND_URL to your public backend URL (or same domain with Nginx proxy).

4. SSL/TLS (optional but recommended):
   - Use Certbot to obtain and install certificates on Nginx.
   - Update Nginx to listen on 443 and redirect HTTP to HTTPS.

5. Monitoring and logs:
   - Use systemd journal for backend logs:
     ```sh
     journalctl -u utorawards-backend -f
     ```
   - Nginx access/error logs in /var/log/nginx.

6. Email configuration:
   - Backend requires Gmail app password in EMAIL_PASSWORD.
   - Ensure “Less secure app access” alternative via app passwords is set.
   - Confirm EMAIL_USER/EMAIL_PASSWORD can send emails; verify SMTP connectivity.

7. Database:
   - Default uses SQLite file via Prisma. For production durability, consider PostgreSQL.
   - If migrating DB:
     - Update [backend/prisma/schema.prisma](backend/prisma/schema.prisma)
     - Run:
       ```sh
       npx prisma generate
       npx prisma migrate deploy
       ```

ii. Environment summary:
- Single VM: Ubuntu 20.04 LTS
- Node.js 18+
- Nginx serving built frontend and proxying API to local Express backend
- SQLite (default) or PostgreSQL (optional)
- Gmail SMTP credentials for password reset emails

## Quick Start (Local Dev)

- Backend:
  ```sh
  cd backend
  npm install
  npx prisma migrate deploy
  npm run seed
  node index.js 3000
  ```
- Frontend:
  ```sh
  cd frontend
  npm install
  echo "VITE_BACKEND_URL=http://localhost:3000" > .env
  npm run dev
  ```

Open http://localhost:5173 and log in using seeded users.